<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Economic Outlook on Daily Deep Think</title><link>https://blog.baifan.site/en/tags/economic-outlook/</link><description>Recent content in Economic Outlook on Daily Deep Think</description><generator>Hugo -- gohugo.io</generator><language>en</language><managingEditor>blog@baifan.site (ByF)</managingEditor><webMaster>blog@baifan.site (ByF)</webMaster><copyright>CC BY-NC 4.0</copyright><lastBuildDate>Mon, 22 Dec 2025 20:00:00 +0800</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://blog.baifan.site/en/tags/economic-outlook/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>The Economist, November 15, 2025</title><link>https://blog.baifan.site/en/economist-20251115-taiwan-boom/</link><pubDate>Mon, 22 Dec 2025 20:00:00 +0800</pubDate><author>blog@baifan.site (ByF)</author><guid>https://blog.baifan.site/en/economist-20251115-taiwan-boom/</guid><description>&lt;figure class="my-6 flex flex-col items-center"&gt;&#10; &lt;img src="https://blog.baifan.site/pictures/te/economist-2025-11-15-cover.png" alt="The Economist cover, November 15, 2025" style="max-width: 500px;" class="rounded-lg shadow-md mx-auto center" loading="lazy" /&gt;&#10; &#10; &lt;figcaption class="mt-2 text-center text-sm text-neutral-500 dark:text-neutral-400 italic"&gt;The Economist cover, November 15, 2025&lt;/figcaption&gt;&#10; &#10;&lt;/figure&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Haven&amp;rsquo;t had time to read it yet — dropping the link here first.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;hr&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Download this issue of The Economist&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="my-6 rounded-lg border-l-4 border-sky-500 bg-sky-50 dark:bg-sky-950/20 p-4 shadow-sm not-prose"&gt;&#10; &#10; &lt;div class="font-bold mb-2 flex items-center gap-2 text-sky-900 dark:text-sky-200"&gt;&#10; &lt;span&gt;EPUB format&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;/div&gt;&#10; &#10; &lt;div class="prose dark:prose-invert text-neutral-800 dark:text-neutral-200 text-base leading-relaxed max-w-none"&gt;&#10; &lt;a href="https://blog.baifan.site/files/te/TE-2025-11-15.change" &gt;TE-2025-11-15.epub&lt;/a&gt;&#10; &lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;</description></item><item><title>When the World Reshuffles: The Economist, Nov 8, 2025</title><link>https://blog.baifan.site/en/economist-2025-11-world-rebalancing/</link><pubDate>Tue, 21 Oct 2025 20:00:00 +0800</pubDate><author>blog@baifan.site (ByF)</author><guid>https://blog.baifan.site/en/economist-2025-11-world-rebalancing/</guid><description>&lt;figure class="my-6 flex flex-col items-center"&gt;&#10; &lt;img src="https://blog.baifan.site/pictures/te/economist-2025-11-08-cover.png" alt="The Economist cover, November 8, 2025" style="max-width: 00px;" class="rounded-lg shadow-md mx-auto center" loading="lazy" /&gt;&#10; &#10; &lt;figcaption class="mt-2 text-center text-sm text-neutral-500 dark:text-neutral-400 italic"&gt;The Economist cover, November 8, 2025: Rebalancing the World&lt;/figcaption&gt;&#10; &#10;&lt;/figure&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The Economist&lt;/em&gt; has always excelled at using polished prose to gloss over savage fractures, dressing up the disintegration of the postwar free-trade architecture and superpower zero-sum warfare as a dignified &amp;ldquo;Rebalancing the World.&amp;rdquo; Peel back the magazine&amp;rsquo;s glossy rhetoric, however, and one confronts an unyielding reality: the high priests of globalization are boarding up their doors, tariff iron curtains are slamming down, and major economies are locking each other in a death grip over industrial subsidies and zero-sum geopolitical spheres.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>